	(text "Discrete Blackmer VCA - 8-transistor log/antilog gain cell (after Hebert, AES preprint 4055, Fig. 4)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 35.56 20.32 0)
		(effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "cfc72cd6-5c62-5bc2-aca8-5f74a0758593"))
	(text "Gain = 0 dB at EC+ = 0 V;  control law about +5.9 mV/dB at EC+ (positive voltage increases gain), drive EC+ from a low-impedance source.\nPin-compatible with the THAT 2181 (SIP-8): current in at IN (virtual earth), current out at OUT; the host supplies the input resistor and I-V converter.\nCore idle current about 20 uA, set by the bias generator;  R10 sets the standing current (about 2 mA)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 35.56 26.67 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "23c8fef3-fe34-51f0-9335-a2091517ab39"))
	(text "INPUT AMPLIFIER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 132.08 43.18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "e155ac8b-8ecd-5c1c-b72e-f283197a0064"))
	(text "GAIN CELL" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 213.36 43.18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "dfb1c83b-af91-5a23-91c6-45464ef49794"))
	(text "BIAS GENERATOR" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 281.94 43.18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c30ec81e-1c6f-5b6b-ae8a-78ed0638da81"))
	(text "Matched pairs (one SOT-457 package each)  /  name in the SPICE model\nQ1A, Q1B  BCM847DS  log / antilog NPN       Q1, Q2\nQ2A, Q2B  BCM857DS  log / antilog PNP       Q3, Q4\nQ3A, Q3B  BCM857DS  lower correction pair   Q5, Q6\nQ4A, Q4B  BCM847DS  upper correction pair   Q7, Q8\nQ5A, Q5B  BCM857DS  bias string             D1, D2\nQ6A, Q6B  BCM847DS  bias string / shunt     D3, QS\nQ7       BC857B    bias shunt              QP" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 35.56 43.18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c1cc00cd-efbe-5b34-a807-130a5d654109"))
	(text "Trim procedure (1 kHz, measure THD at the host output)\n1. RV1: 0 dB gain, 1 Vrms in - null distortion.\n2. RV2: -15 dB gain, 3 Vrms in - null distortion.\n3. Repeat 1 and 2 once.\n4. RV3: EC+ = 0 V - set unity gain.\nR3 / C1 set input-amplifier stability and HF distortion.\nR4-R7 (1R8) cancel transistor bulk resistance." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 35.56 78.74 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "5d0b2289-ac54-5ff4-b034-860e7411853f"))
	(text "Using it in a 2181 socket\nV- (pin 5): the host normally has about 5k1 from this pin to -15 V. Then fit R10 = 0R,\n  leave JP1 open and bring -15 V to J2 on a wire.\n  If the host ties pin 5 straight to -15 V instead: fit R10 = 6k8 and close JP1.\nEC- (pin 3): if the host drives EC-, omit R16, R15 and RV3 (the host sets gain).\nSYM (pin 4): a host symmetry trim adds to RV1; it is not needed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 35.56 261.62 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "0e8b49bc-a59a-5dbb-90e0-ea2111292a72"))
